## Context

PR #316 (ticket 0219) landed the discovery phase + handcuff/scope passes
for skills/fang-audit/. Its gaze ran without the full review-pr/simplify
passes; a post-merge /code-review (7 angles, adversarial verification)
found defects the adherence tests cannot see — they are string-presence
checks, and the defects are runtime-semantics.

**BLOCKS the AEDIST validation run.** Defect 1 fires exactly on
path-prefixed test layouts (Python `tests/` dirs): launched today, the
~3-5M-token AEDIST run would return an empty scope pass, a no-op
priority sort, and an all-n/a three-axis table.

## Confirmed defects (adversarially verified, quoted-line evidence)

1. **Test-identity key mismatch** — dicts written with `base(a.testFile)`
   (basename) but read with raw `BEHAVIORAL[].test` (discovery may return
   `tests/test_foo.py`). Three dead features on path-prefixed repos:
   scope pass never dispatches (`caughtOpsByFile`, ~l.644/649), handcuff
   priority sort is a no-op (`fangByFile`, ~l.625/627), three-axis table
   all-zero (`_file` vs `name`, ~l.778-793). Go repos (bare co-located
   filenames) mask it. Root fix: ONE canonical normalization at the
   l.172 BEHAVIORAL mapping; ban per-site base() on keys.
2. **Empty RUN_TEST passes every gate** — schema has no minLength, the
   post-discovery abort (~l.157) checks only BEHAVIORAL.length, FALLBACKS
   has no RUN_TEST entry. `RUN_TEST:''` → every agent gets a blank test
   command → all mutations trivially "survive" → false-accusation flood.
3. **Precheck gate not enforced** — abort is `gate==='fail'` only;
   PRECHECK_SCHEMA.gate is a bare string (no enum). A real agent
   returning `gate:'skipped'/'Pass'/'unknown'` passes the flakiness gate
   AND leaves `precheckSkipped=false`, masking it in the return value.
   Fix: schema `enum: ['pass','fail']` (Workflow validates + retries on
   mismatch) and require `gate==='pass'` affirmatively.

## Verified advisories (fix in the same sweep)

- Precheck open-skip is invisible in the Markdown report (canary skip
  has a ⏭️ banner; precheck skip only log() + return field). Add the
  mirror banner to the L assembly.
- DISCOVERY_SCHEMA enforces none of the discovery-quality contract:
  `rationale` optional (a glob-derived table passes the only machine
  gate — the banned heuristic returns through the side door), non-1:1
  pairs unprotected. Require rationale; add an adherence test that the
  prompt demands import/call-site evidence.
- Adherence tests are vacuous w.r.t. defect 1 — string-presence checks
  stay green while the features are inert. Add a key-consistency test
  (extract write-keys/read-keys, assert one normalization).
- fangByFile double-counts a file present in both BEHAVIORAL and GUARDS
  (populated from all findings) — filter on `_isGuardFile`.
- Pass-shape is 3 hand-wired copies: applyRules/handcuffRules/scopeRules
  identical template-expanders; skepticize/handcuffSkepticize differ only
  in filter/prompt/schema/label (labels already diverged: testFunc
  dropped from hc-skeptic). Extract expandRules() + runSkeptic() before
  a 4th lens (0183) forces a fifth copy.
- Mechanical agents (precheck, cleanup, churn) run on default Opus while
  skeptics pin sonnet; churn's input (file list) is known at start yet it
  waits for all passes. Pin cheap models; dispatch churn concurrently.
- SKILL.md drift: the git-erg reference reproduction now needs
  undocumented GUARDS+UNTRACKED_SEED overrides (discovery cannot derive
  them); "Python adapter ... if one exists" implies an adapter
  test-quality.py does not have (`--adapter` choices: go only) — a user
  wiring PRECHECK_CMD manually gets argparse exit 2 on every run.

## Relevant files

- skills/fang-audit/fang-audit.js — all defects
- skills/fang-audit/SKILL.md — doc drift items
- tests/test_fang_audit_skill.py — vacuous-test fixes, new guards

## Exit criteria

- [ ] One canonical test-identity normalization (BEHAVIORAL mapping
      site); scope pass, handcuff sort, and three-axis table verified
      live on a path-prefixed fixture (tests/ subdir layout)
- [ ] RUN_TEST validated non-empty before fan-out (schema minLength
      and/or truthiness abort)
- [ ] PRECHECK_SCHEMA.gate enum ['pass','fail']; abort requires
      affirmative pass; real-agent 'skipped' cannot mask as a pass
- [ ] Precheck skip banner in the Markdown report, mirroring canary
- [ ] Adherence test catches a write-key/read-key normalization split
      (must FAIL on the pre-fix code)
- [ ] Advisories addressed or explicitly waived in the PR body
- [ ] make check passes
